From fa71cc1192eece19c42c1c82271aac9201fa22dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: josephlyimo <josephlyimo201@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 09:23:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: eliminate duplicate path generation when Redis queue is
 active

- Split generatePath() into createLearningPath() (fast phase: one Gemini
  call + Goal/LearningPath rows) and processLearningPathTopics() (slow
  phase: per-topic YouTube sourcing). generatePath() remains as a
  convenience wrapper composing both, for local dev.
- pathGeneration.queue.ts now calls createLearningPath() once, then either
  hands the already-generated syllabus to the BullMQ worker (production)
  or runs processLearningPathTopics() inline (local dev) - never both.
  Previously, queuePathGeneration() called the old generatePath() (which
  started the full pipeline as a side effect) AND enqueued a worker job
  that called it again, doubling every Gemini call and YouTube sourcing
  pass, and leaving an orphaned duplicate Goal/LearningPath row per
  request whenever Redis was configured.
- Removed unused InMemoryQueueJob interface (queue.ts).

fix: remove explicit 'any' types from getPath.ts and getUserPaths.ts

Replaced any-typed callback params with local interfaces describing the
query result shapes actually used, resolving the eslint
no-explicit-any errors on these two live/active files.
